\section{Modifying results}

We have two alternatives: add a new result or update an existing result draft.

\subsection{[[create_result_JSON]]}

This method is used to create a new result.
This result will be a draft.
It must later be finalized and then attested.

Note that since this is a new result, we must provide the [[StudieresultatUID]] 
where we want to add the result.
When we've done this, we'll get a [[ResultatUID]] back in the response.
From then on, it's the [[ResultatUID]] that's interesting.

Note also that we can use [[course_instance_id]] as [[component_id]], this will 
set the result on the whole course.
<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def create_result_JSON(self,
      student_id: str, course_instance_id: str, component_id: str,
      grade_id: int, date: str,
      project_title: str | None = None) -> dict:
  """
  Creates a new result
  """
  try:
    return self.post_query(
      f"/resultat/internal/resultat/student/{student_id}"
      f"/kursinstans/{course_instance_id}"
      f"/utbildningsinstans/{component_id}"
      f"/skapa",
      {
        "Betygsgrad": grade_id,
        "Examinationsdatum": date,
        "Projekttitel": project_title
      }
    )
  except LadokServerError as err:
    raise LadokServerError(f"LADOK server error when creating result for "
                           f"student {student_id} on component {component_id}: "
                           f"{err}") from err
  except LadokAPIError as err:
    raise LadokAPIError(f"Failed to create result for student {student_id} "
                        f"on component {component_id}: {err}") from err
@

These write tests change a real student's record in the test environment,
so each test must leave the record as it found it, also when it fails
halfway.
A result goes through up to three states, and each one needs its own step to
undo:
\begin{description}
\item[Draft] is removed with [[remove_result_draft_JSON]].
\item[Finalized] must first be turned back into a draft with
  [[finalized_result_to_draft_JSON]], and then removed.
\item[Attested] needs the examiner to remove the attestation, which LADOK
  guards with a forced new login, MFA included.
  LADOK's API allows it, but ladok3 does not implement attestation yet; the
  flow and a plan are in issue~63 on GitHub.
\end{description}
[[remove_lab_result]] walks the test student's LAB1 result back through these
steps, whatever state it is in.
It reads the state from LADOK rather than from the test, since a failed test
may have stopped between two steps.
An attested result it leaves alone, failing and saying what to do by hand.
The tests never attest, so that only happens if someone attests a result
that a failed run left behind.

Each test gets its result from a fixture: [[draft_result]] creates a draft,
and [[finalized_result]] finalizes that draft.
The fixture calls [[remove_lab_result]] both before creating the result, to
clear anything an aborted run left behind, and after the test, also when the
test failed.
An earlier version instead chained the tests through module variables: one
test created the result, the next updated it, and so on, with the last one
removing it.
A single test could not run on its own, and a failure in the middle left the
result in LADOK.
<<test functions>>=
datintro_student_uid = "76291c55-d24a-11ea-a4db-82cca4dd4b3e"
datintro_instance_id = "2179e02c-d6b5-11e8-8fd5-cf9d2c5c41ba"
datintro_LAB1_id = "385a4428-73d8-11e8-b4e0-063f9afb40e3"

DRAFT = 1
FINALIZED = 2
PASS_GRADE_ID = 131663
FAIL_GRADE_ID = 131658

def lab_result(ladok):
  """Return the test student's LAB1 result on DATINTRO as a pair: the work
  copy (draft or finalized) and the attested result, each None if absent."""
  education_id = ladok.course_instance_JSON(
    datintro_instance_id)["UtbildningUID"]
  results = ladok.student_results_JSON(datintro_student_uid, education_id)
  for version in results["Kursversioner"]:
    for module in version["VersionensModuler"]:
      if module["UtbildningsinstansUID"] == datintro_LAB1_id:
        wrapper = module.get("ResultatPaUtbildning", {})
        return (wrapper.get("Arbetsunderlag"),
                wrapper.get("SenastAttesteradeResultat"))
  return None, None

def remove_lab_result(ladok):
  """Walk the test student's LAB1 result back to nothing: a finalized
  result goes back to draft, a draft is removed.  Fail if it is attested,
  since ladok3 can't remove attestations yet (issue 63); a draft on top of
  the attested result is then left too."""
  draft, attested = lab_result(ladok)
  if attested:
    pytest.fail(f"LAB1 result {attested['Uid']} of the test student is "
                "attested; remove the attestation in LADOK's web "
                "interface, then rerun")
  if draft is None:
    return
  if draft["ProcessStatus"] == FINALIZED:
    draft = ladok.finalized_result_to_draft_JSON(
      draft["Uid"], draft["SenasteResultatandring"])
  ladok.remove_result_draft_JSON(draft["Uid"])

@pytest.fixture
def draft_result(ladok):
  remove_lab_result(ladok)
  result = ladok.create_result_JSON(
    datintro_student_uid, datintro_instance_id, datintro_LAB1_id,
    PASS_GRADE_ID, "2022-11-29")
  yield result
  remove_lab_result(ladok)

@pytest.fixture
def finalized_result(ladok, draft_result):
  return ladok.finalize_result_JSON(
    draft_result["Uid"], draft_result["SenasteResultatandring"],
    reporter_id)
@

