\section{[[examination_occasions_JSON]]}

Examination occasions (\emph{aktivitetstillfälle}) are listed via the
[[resultat]] service.  A single occasion covers one exam event, e.g.\
a written examination of course SH1014 on a specific date.  Walking
all pages with [[_all_pages]] (\cref{Pagination}) matters here because
courses that have run for a long time accumulate many occasions and a
fixed page size will hide older ones.

We use the search that LADOK's own web client uses,
[[aktivitetstillfalle/filtrera/lattvikt]] (\enquote{lightweight}).
Until LADOK's update of 20 October 2026 we used
[[aktivitetstillfalle/filtrera]], with the same parameters.
Since that update, it refuses the course code with a validation error
(\enquote{Incorrect format} for a \enquote{Unique identifier}), so it
evidently wants a UID that the web client does not send.
The lightweight search takes the course code and gives the same list, with
somewhat fewer fields.

Key fields returned for each occasion:
\begin{description}
\item[ [[Uid]] ] Occasion UID, required for result retrieval.
\item[ [[Aktivitetstillfallesalternativ]] ] The alternatives of the
  occasion, each with its examination date(s) in [[Datumperiod]], as
  [[Startdatum]] / [[Slutdatum]], and its times in [[Starttid]] /
  [[Sluttid]].
\item[ [[AntalAnmalda]] ] Number of registered students.
\item[ [[KurstillfalleUIDer]] ] Course-round UIDs associated with this
  occasion; pass these to [[occasion_results_JSON]].
\item[ [[AktivitetstillfallestypID]] ] The type of the occasion, such as a
  written examination, as an ID among the activity-occasion types
  ([[aktivitetstillfallestyp_JSON]]).
  The old search also gave the type's name, in
  [[AktivitetstillfallestypBenamning]].
\end{description}
<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def examination_occasions_JSON(self, course_code: str) -> list:
  """Return all examination occasions for a course."""
  return self._all_pages(lambda page, limit: self.get_query(
    f"/resultat/internal/aktivitetstillfalle/filtrera/lattvikt"
    f"?kurskod={course_code}&page={page}&limit={limit}",
    "application/vnd.ladok-resultat+json"
  ))
@

The test checks the fields that the description above promises, for every
occasion, and that the course's known occasion is among them.
<<test functions>>=
def test_examination_occasions_JSON(ladok) -> None:
  occasions = ladok.examination_occasions_JSON("SH1014")
  assert len(occasions) > 0
  occasion_uids = [o["Uid"] for o in occasions]
  assert SH1014_occasion_id in occasion_uids
  for occasion in occasions:
    assert isinstance(occasion["KurstillfalleUIDer"], list)
    assert isinstance(occasion["AktivitetstillfallestypID"], int)
