\section{[[grade_scales_all_text]]}

[[grade_scales_JSON]] (\cref{GradeScalesJSON}) returns the standard
grade scales the LADOK JSON variant exposes --- but not all of them.
Empirically, the same endpoint
[[/kataloginformation/internal/grunddata/betygsskala]] queried with an
XML [[Accept]] header returns a strictly larger set: it includes
institution-specific scales such as KTH's seven-point A--F scale that
the JSON variant omits.  Why the JSON representation filters and the
XML one doesn't is undocumented, and the situation may change ---
future maintainers should periodically retry the JSON endpoint and
collapse the two methods into one if the asymmetry goes away.

We deliberately return the raw response \emph{text} rather than parse
the XML here.  Parsing belongs in the caller because (a) consumers of
this method already need to walk a heterogeneous mix of standard and
institution-specific scales, and (b) we don't want to add an
[[xml.etree]] dependency to this module just to expose one endpoint
variant.  The thin [[get_query_text]] helper carries the request,
re-using [[get_query]]'s session and error mapping so a failure here
raises the same [[LadokServerError]] / [[LadokAPIError]] callers
already handle.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def grade_scales_all_text(self) -> str:
