\section{Shared helper: [[_utbildningstillfalle_JSON]]}

In LADOK, [[utbildningstillfalle]] (\enquote{education round}) is the
umbrella term that covers both \emph{course} rounds
([[kurstillfalle]]) and \emph{programme} rounds
([[kurspaketeringstillfalle]]) --- both kinds are stored as
[[utbildningstillfalle]] records by the
[[utbildningsinformation]] service, and one endpoint serves both:
\[
  \texttt{GET /utbildningsinformation/internal/utbildningstillfalle/\{uid\}}.
\]
The two public wrappers below ([[program_round_by_uid_JSON]] and
[[course_round_utbildningsinformation_JSON]]) call this same endpoint;
their value is in the \emph{intent} they expose at the call site --- a
reader who sees [[program_round_by_uid_JSON(uid)]] knows the caller
expects programme-round metadata, not just \enquote{some
utbildningstillfälle record}.  We keep the wrappers thin so the URL
and Accept-header live in exactly one place; if LADOK ever
restructures this endpoint, only the helper changes.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def _utbildningstillfalle_JSON(self, uid: str) -> dict:
  """Fetch an utbildningstillfalle record (course or programme round).

  Internal helper.  Uses GET
  /utbildningsinformation/internal/utbildningstillfalle/{uid}.

  Most callers should use the intent-revealing wrappers
  program_round_by_uid_JSON or course_round_utbildningsinformation_JSON
  instead of calling this directly.
  """
  return self.get_query(
    f"/utbildningsinformation/internal/utbildningstillfalle/{uid}",
    "application/vnd.ladok-utbildningsinformation+json",
  )
