\subsection{Participations in a state}

LADOK does answer the second form.
The student resource links to five views of the student's participations,
one per state, at
[[/studiedeltagande/internal/tillfallesdeltagande/]]\emph{state}[[/student/{uid}]]:
\begin{description}
\item[{[[pagaende]]}] the ongoing ones;
\item[{[[kommande]]}] the upcoming ones;
\item[{[[oavslutade]]}] the unfinished ones, whose round has ended without
  the student completing the course;
\item[{[[avslutade]]}] the completed ones;
\item[{[[avbrott]]}] the ones the student broke off.
\end{description}
They need no special roles, cohm found, and they answer like
[[registrations_JSON]]: a [[Tillfallesdeltaganden]] list of entries of the
same shape.
(A completed participation also carries its [[Godkannandedatum]].)
The views never overlap, but together they need not hold every
participation: a student who withdrew before the round started
([[aterbud]]) or broke off early ([[tidigtavbrott]]) is in none of them, nor
is one who never started a round that has ended.

We use LADOK's Swedish names for the states, since they are what LADOK calls
them and what the paths contain; the classes give them English names
(\cref{CourseRegistrationState}).
<<constants>>=
PARTICIPATION_STATES = ("pagaende", "kommande", "oavslutade", "avslutade",
                        "avbrott")
@

[[student_participations_JSON]] returns these views as LADOK gives them,
and every participation through [[registrations_JSON]] when no state is
given; [[student_course_participations_JSON]] above keeps the courses of
either.
The student classes use this method directly, since they keep every
registration that [[registrations_JSON]] returns
(\cref{StudentCourses}).
A state that LADOK does not have would be sent to it as a path that does not
exist, and its 404 would tell the caller less than we can, so we refuse it
first, with a [[ValueError]] that lists the states there are.
<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def student_participations_JSON(self, student_uid: str,
                                state: str | None = None) -> list:
  """Return a student's participations, all of them or those in a state.

  Without `state`, the same as registrations_JSON(student_uid).  With
  `state`, one of PARTICIPATION_STATES ("pagaende", "kommande",
  "oavslutade", "avslutade", "avbrott"), LADOK's view of the
  participations in that state.  Raises ValueError for any other state.
  """
  if state is None:
    return self.registrations_JSON(student_uid)
  check_participation_state(state)
  data = self.get_query(
    f"/studiedeltagande/internal/tillfallesdeltagande/{state}"
    f"/student/{student_uid}",
    "application/vnd.ladok-studiedeltagande+json")
  try:
    return data["Tillfallesdeltaganden"]
  except KeyError as err:
    err.add_note(f"Response data: {data}")
    raise LadokAPIError(
      f"Unexpected response format when fetching {state} participations "
      f"for student {student_uid}: missing 'Tillfallesdeltaganden' key"
    ) from err
<<functions>>=
def check_participation_state(state) -> None:
  """Raise ValueError unless `state` is one of PARTICIPATION_STATES."""
  if state not in PARTICIPATION_STATES:
    raise ValueError(f"unknown participation state {state!r}, expected "
                     f"one of {', '.join(PARTICIPATION_STATES)}")
@

An unknown state must be refused before any request is sent.
The [[offline_ladok]] session cannot reach LADOK, so a request would fail the
test with a network error instead.
<<test functions>>=
@pytest.mark.parametrize("state", ["ongoing", "Pagaende", ""])
def test_unknown_participation_state_is_refused(offline_ladok, state) -> None:
  with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="pagaende"):
