\section{[[fetch_linked_uri_JSON]]}

Several Ladok responses include hypermedia links whose [[href]] values are full
URIs pointing to the API host (e.g.\
\texttt{https://api.test.ladok.se:443/utbildningsinformation/\ldots}).  This
helper strips the scheme and host so the request can be routed through the
GUI proxy, which is what carries our session credentials --- the API host
itself doesn't see them.

We validate the input rather than letting string surgery silently chew on
arbitrary text.  The reason: if [[uri]] is malformed or points at some host
other than LADOK's API, the caller would proxy a request for data that did not
come from LADOK at all.  By rejecting non-URI input up front and insisting that
the host matches the current environment's LADOK API host, we keep the helper
as narrow as the situations that actually call it.

The default content-type is left to [[get_query]] (which negotiates
JSON broadly via [[self.headers]]).  Earlier we hard-coded
[[utbildningsinformation+json]], but the helper is meant to follow
\emph{any} hypermedia link --- baking one service's content-type in
silently mis-described links from the [[resultat]] or [[studiedeltagande]]
services and is exactly the kind of \enquote{convenient default} that
hides bugs.  Callers who really do know the content-type should pass
it explicitly.

<<LadokSession data methods>>=
def fetch_linked_uri_JSON(self, uri: str,
                          content_type: str | None = None) -> dict | list:
  """Fetch a Ladok hypermedia URI via the GUI proxy.

  Strips the scheme and host from uri, then delegates to get_query().
  Use this when a Ladok response embeds a full URI in a link array, e.g.
  https://api.test.ladok.se:443/utbildningsinformation/internal/struktur/{uid}.

  Raises LadokValidationError if uri is not an http(s) URI for the current
  LADOK API host.
  """
  parsed = urllib.parse.urlparse(uri)
  if parsed.scheme not in ("http", "https") or not parsed.path:
    raise LadokValidationError(
      f"fetch_linked_uri_JSON: not an http(s) URI with a path: {uri!r}")
  expected_host = urllib.parse.urlparse(
    self.base_url.replace("start.", "api.", 1)).hostname
  if parsed.hostname != expected_host:
    raise LadokValidationError(
      f"fetch_linked_uri_JSON: unexpected host {parsed.hostname!r}, "
      f"expected {expected_host!r}")
  path = parsed.path
  if parsed.query:
    path += f"?{parsed.query}"
  if content_type is None:
    return self.get_query(path)
  return self.get_query(path, content_type)
@

The validation test ensures a non-URI input is rejected up front
(rather than silently issuing a partial-path GET).  The happy-path
test constructs a URI in the same shape as a real LADOK hypermedia
link and verifies it resolves through the proxy.
<<test functions>>=
def test_fetch_linked_uri_JSON_rejects_non_uri(offline_ladok) -> None:
  with pytest.raises(ladok3.LadokValidationError):
    offline_ladok.fetch_linked_uri_JSON("not a uri")

def test_fetch_linked_uri_JSON_rejects_wrong_host(offline_ladok) -> None:
  with pytest.raises(ladok3.LadokValidationError):
    offline_ladok.fetch_linked_uri_JSON(
      f"https://example.com/utbildningsinformation/internal/"
      f"utbildningsinstans/{dasak_instance_id}")

def test_fetch_linked_uri_JSON_follows_link(ladok) -> None:
  uri = ("https://api.test.ladok.se:443/utbildningsinformation"
         f"/internal/utbildningsinstans/{dasak_instance_id}")
  record = ladok.fetch_linked_uri_JSON(
    uri, content_type="application/vnd.ladok-utbildningsinformation+json")
  assert record["Uid"] == dasak_instance_id
